 "verdict": "consistent once read from the cipher: 72 signs = 72 letters, 19 groups = 19 words, one letter per shape (68/68 repeated); the first verse is من تحرز كافات الشتا كفاه مع حسن عطيته بمن ينشاه (the \"kafs of winter\" the compiler's comment names), not من خمر زكا فاق الشتا ... عفته ... انشاه; ن has two shapes (ዋ, Π), ت two (Δ-stem once)",
 "notes": "Rows 8-12 of image 0084_0138: 16 + 14 + 14 + 17 + 11 = 72, as the record; اموره runs over the line end (ا م | و ر ه). Plain 1.3x half-line zooms, 1.8-2.3x on the first line and look-alikes. The second verse keys without conflict (record confirmed, with آمره in 4 signs as the record says); with that key the first line's groups (2, 4, 5, 5) read من تحرز كافات الشتا: the sin-teeth-on-a-loop sign is ت in سلمت and in all four, the J-hook ح as in حسن, the e-loop ر as in اموره and آمره, V ز; كافات is the \"kafs of winter\" (the seven things beginning with kaf that protect from winter), which the compiler's comment on 67v l.5 calls كاف الشتا. On l.9 the 5-sign word is ع ط ي ت ه = عطيته (\"his gift\"; the pentagon ط and the triangle-on-a-stem ت are singletons there, the ي is the barred triangle of الى); on l.10 the word after بمن starts with that ي: ينشاه, not انشاه. Read: \"whoever guards against the kafs of winter, it suffices him, with the goodness of His gift to whom He raises up\"; tentative in the singleton letters ط and the second ت."
}